# Project Overview

AIF Handoff is an autonomous task-management system with a Kanban UI and
runtime-routed AI workflows. Tasks move through Backlog, Planning, Plan Ready,
Implementing, Review, Done, and Verified. The product coordinates planning,
implementation, review, security review, runtime profile selection, chat, MCP
sync, and optional automatic review/rework loops.

# Tech Stack

- Language: TypeScript with ES modules.
- Monorepo: npm workspaces plus Turborepo.
- API: Hono, Node server, WebSocket.
- Frontend: React, Vite, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query, dnd-kit.
- Database: SQLite with better-sqlite3 and drizzle-orm.
- Runtime layer: `@aif/runtime` with Claude, Codex, OpenRouter, OpenCode, and external modules.
- Agent process: runtime-neutral coordinator with polling and WebSocket wake channel.
- Tests: Vitest and Testing Library; Playwright is used for web performance/e2e flows.

# Package Map

- `packages/shared`: shared contracts, schema, state machine, env, constants, logger, browser exports.
- `packages/data`: centralized data-access API for all SQLite reads and writes.
- `packages/runtime`: provider/runtime contracts, registry, capabilities, profile resolution, adapters.
- `packages/api`: REST, WebSocket, settings, projects, tasks, chat, runtime profile routes.
- `packages/web`: React app, Kanban/list UI, task detail, chat, project/runtime settings, UI primitives.
- `packages/agent`: coordinator, planner, implementer, reviewer, watchdogs, wake channel, runtime execution.
- `packages/mcp`: MCP task sync server and tools.

